## Back-End — Clean Architecture & DDD (Laravel)

When changing **tradeup-api**, follow [Back-End Architecture](../../../docs/back-end/architecture.md): **Domain** (entities, value objects, repository interfaces), **Application** (use cases, DTOs, orchestration), **Infrastructure** (Eloquent implementations, integrations, bindings), **Delivery** (routes, controllers, jobs — thin).

**Do**

- Add behavior as **use cases** under `app/Application/.../UseCases/`; controllers map HTTP → DTO → use case → response.
- Define **repository (or port) interfaces** inward (`Domain` or `Application`); implement in `app/Infrastructure/...`.
- Keep **domain** free of Eloquent, HTTP, and framework facades.

**Don’t**

- Put **business rules** only in controllers or FormRequests.
- Use **Eloquent models as ubiquitous domain objects** across layers; map at the infrastructure edge when needed.
- Call **`DB::`, `Http::`, filesystem** directly from use cases; inject an interface and implement in infrastructure.

**Composition:** bind interfaces to implementations in service providers (composition root). Prefer naming use cases after **business intent** (`RegisterUser`), not framework roles.

